{
  "id": "COMPOUND:15637 - PROTEIN:5011",
  "verbalization": "Oleiferin C appears to have a shared target relationship with HCC1937 through multiple pathways, all of which converge on the mitochondrial thioredoxin protein. This protein is targeted by several compounds, including Cyclizidine, Isodaucene, and Oleamide, all of which ultimately lead to HCC1937. The consistent involvement of thioredoxin in these interactions suggests a potential mechanism where Oleiferin C may modulate mitochondrial function, influencing cellular processes that ultimately affect HCC1937. The presence of multiple distinct targets (Cyclizidine, Isodaucene, and Oleamide) further supports the idea that Oleiferin C exerts its effects through diverse pathways, possibly by regulating thioredoxin activity. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of thioredoxin in mediating the relationship between Oleiferin C and HCC1937, emphasizing the role of this protein in the biological response to Oleiferin C.",
